course: dictionary
lesson: 1315
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word cage can mean different things, so check the words around it. «The bird in its cage sobbing to be let out» tells you a cage is a box that keeps a bird inside, because the bird wants to be let out.
explain: Cage can also be a verb, an action word. To cage an animal means to put it in a cage. If you read «they cage the parrot at night», someone is doing something, so cage is a verb here. Ask yourself: is cage a thing, or something someone does?
explain: Cage can name a part of your body too. «Twelve pairs of ribs curve round from the spine like a cage» uses the word like to compare: your ribs are shaped like a cage. The rib cage is not a box with bars. It is the set of bones that guards your heart and lungs.
fact: A cage is a box or room made of bars or wire that keeps animals or birds inside.
fact: To cage an animal means to put it, or keep it, in a cage.
fact: The rib cage is the set of bones round your chest that protects your heart and lungs.
fact: Cage is a noun (cage, cages) and also a verb (caged, caging).
fact: Pets such as hamsters and birds live in cages, and their cages need cleaning.
exercise: «The bird in its cage sobbing to be let out.» What is the cage in this sentence? | A drawn blind over a window | *A box of bars or wire that keeps the bird inside | A bone in the chest | A kind of cart full of sardine tins
exercise: «Think of a parrot climbing its cage.» What does cage mean here? | To put a parrot in a cart | *A box made of bars or wire, where a parrot lives | A sort of climbing tree | To sing loudly
exercise: The zookeepers cage the lions at night. What does cage mean here? | To let the lions run free | *To put the lions in a cage | To wash | To feed the lions their dinner
test: «Twelve pairs of ribs curve round from the spine like a cage, guarding the heart and lungs.» What is the rib cage? | A bar of soap | A kind of cage for hamsters | A box for a pet bird | *The bones round your chest that protect your heart and lungs
test: Which sentence uses cage as a verb? | The cages were empty after the rescue. | *Nadia will cage the rabbit before the vet arrives. | Her rib cage hurt when she laughed. | The bird-cage hung by the window.
exam: «The bird in its cage sobbing to be let out.» Why is the bird sobbing? | It is singing a happy song | It has just laid an egg | *It is trapped and wants to be free | It is cold and wants a blanket
